---
description: UI component and styling conventions
globs: "**/*.{ts,tsx,css,module.css}"
alwaysApply: true
---

- Search first: reuse, extend, or compose existing components before creating new ones.
- Keep reusable UI semantic, accessible, business-logic-free, and mobile-first.

Shared theme policies live in `ui/common/src/design-system/theme/`. Consult `ui/web/src/design-system/Overview.mdx` and the relevant foundations once per task; reuse already-loaded guidance:
- Variants and interaction states: `Appearance.mdx`.
- Palettes and shades: `colors/Colors.mdx` and `Theming.mdx`.

Shared reusable components require a common API/value logic in `@ui/common` and thin renderers in both `@web-ui` and `@mobile-ui`.

Use common constants/policies for renderer and shared story defaults (`DEFAULT_SIZE`, `DEFAULT_COLOR`, variant defaults, etc.), not equivalent literals. Explicit non-default examples may override them. Galleries start from the shared story size and follow the selected size, not the first option.

### Component Structure

Split components by meaningful visual purpose, interaction, styling, or state. Parents compose; leaves render.

Name files after their components. Tiny private helpers may stay with their only parent; component-local constants and helpers stay local.

Keep platform stories current. Public reusable components need `Playground with Live code editor` and `Gallery`; infer `argTypes` except non-inferable controls/mappings.

Use shared gallery primitives for color/variant/size coverage, showing one selected size rather than looping over sizes. Add sections only for other dimensions, such as shape or orientation.

All component Gallery stories must compose the platform's shared gallery primitives for color, variant, and size coverage instead of building a parallel matrix. Show one selected size at a time; never loop over sizes. Compose separate sections only for dimensions the shared gallery does not cover, such as shape or orientation.

Reserve final layout dimensions before optional or asynchronous content appears; toggling content must not move surrounding UI.

Buttons use square corners by default. Circle and hexagon buttons are icon-only and require an accessible label.

### Web
- Apps and gears must use components from `@web-ui` when an appropriate component exists.
- Inside `@web-ui`, use native semantic elements (`<hr>`, `<button>`, `<nav>`, `<label>`, etc.) instead of generic `<div>` elements.
- Interactive elements must support keyboard use and include ARIA attributes when needed.
- Use CSS modules.
- Class names use kebab-case.
- Use `className` instead of inline `style`.
- Use inline `style` only for runtime-computed values that cannot use classes or CSS variables.
- Use CSS variables for theming.
- Never use `!important`.

### Mobile
- Use `StyleSheet.create` for styles.
- Define `StyleSheet.create` before props and components.
- Do not use CSS modules or CSS custom properties.
